{
 "figure": "template_changes",
 "caption": "Histories from the original five scenarios, helpful or dismissive supplied turns 1-2, then the prohibition and question, in five chat formats. Left: forced readout \"By the way,\" + 48 tokens; routing kept = (dismissive minus helpful rival share among habit-bearing replies) in the format divided by the same gap in the training template; pre-registered bar 0.70. Right: free replies (2,048 tokens) after a helpful history, share of all replies that start the habit; thinking on: 0 of 192 (bee-helper), 1 of 192 (crow-helper). 192 replies per model cell; one training run per model; script-clustered 95% intervals. Thinking also adds the model's own reasoning, which drafts the reply, so template keying is not isolated. Plain-transcript replies are shorter (most stop at a self-written 'User:' turn). The untrained model: 0 habit in every cell.",
